                <pb facs="0587" n="511" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg511"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.151/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-11T10:00:00+02:00">July 11, 1934—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 11—6:46 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. Your 42, July 6, 3 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs assures that no
                    action will be taken against Ulen and Company in the matter of the $100,000
                    before the arrival of Gausmann.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
